It almost sounds like SRM is set to autoboot.  Experts out there might know of a 
different method to get around autoboot, but the only reliable method I ever 
could get to work was to disconnect the hard drive - at that point the boot 
would fail and it would fall back to SRM.

(Some people claim to have luck with madly hitting CTRL-C before it starts 
booting - but I've never had that work.)

Once in SRM, you need to do "set auto_action halt", this should then make sure 
that the next time you start up, you end up at the SRM prompt and can then 
follow all the usual directions of how to boot off of CD.

- Rob

